-- title:
--   T/I ≅ ℤ/n at prime level (Mazur II.9.7)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime. Write $\mathbb{T}_p$ for the Hecke algebra at level $p$ in weight $2$, namely the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅` of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of the space of cusp forms of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(p)$ generated by the Hecke generators with empty excluded set, and let `intLattice p 2` be the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of those cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers. Restricting endomorphisms to this lattice gives a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{T}_p$ into $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{Z}}(\mathtt{intLattice }p\,2)$, whose image is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅`; the theorem concerns the corange map `latticeRestrictHom p ∅` onto that image. Let $\mathbb{T} = \mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ be the abstract Hecke algebra, evaluated into $\mathbb{T}_p$ by `heckeEvalForms p 2`, which sends $X_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise, and let `eisensteinIdeal p` be the kernel of the specialisation $X_\ell \mapsto 1$ for $\ell \mid p$, $X_\ell \mapsto 1 + \ell$ otherwise. The assertion is that the quotient of `heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅` by the ideal generated by the image of `eisensteinIdeal p` under the evaluation map followed by the restriction map has exactly $(p-1)/\gcd(p-1,12)$ elements, i.e. the numerator of $(p-1)/12$.
--
--   This is Mazur's computation of the order of $\mathbb{T}/I$ at prime level, Proposition II.9.7 of the Eisenstein ideal paper, here phrased on the integral lattice side and as an equality of cardinalities rather than as an isomorphism $\mathbb{T}/I \cong \mathbb{Z}/n$. It is used to show that the Eisenstein maximal ideal at a prime not dividing the numerator of $(p-1)/12$ contributes no torsion.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_eisensteinIdeal_eq_eisensteinNumerator.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeLocal
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeEvalForms
import Definitions.Def_HeckeGalois_EichlerShimura
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_ModularUnit

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open ModularCurve CuspForm

theorem ModularCurve.natCard_heckeLatticeAlgebra_quotient_eisensteinIdeal_eq_eisensteinNumerator
    (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] :
    Nat.card (↥(heckeLatticeAlgebra p ∅) ⧸
        Ideal.map ((latticeRestrictHom p ∅).toRingHom.comp (heckeEvalForms p 2))
          (eisensteinIdeal p)) =
      eisensteinNumerator p := by sorry
